- **Largest of three numbers**: assume the first is largest, compare with the second then the third, keep the bigger.
- **Factorial**: start with result 1 and multiply by every number from 1 to n.
- **Prime test**: a number n > 1 is prime if no integer from 2 to n-1 divides it (checking up to square root of n is enough).
- Always trace the algorithm by hand with a small input before coding.
